# Server API conventions

## Module structure

`server/api/<name>/`: `index.js`, `*.controller.js`, `*.model.js`, optional `*.integration.js`.

## Critical endpoints

- **`POST /api/workouts/upload`** — base64 plist body → `bplist-parser` → JSON array for the client (`workout.controller.js`)
- **`GET /api/airports`** — airport lat/long for twilight logic
- **`GET /pdf`** — serves `server/pdfs/*.pdf` for F12 generation

## Controllers

- Server uses Babel 6 `import`/`export` and Sequelize 3 promise style (`.then/.catch`) consistent with the file
- Register new routers in `server/routes.js`

## Firebase

Not initialized in server code yet. Credentials file: `server/firebase.json` (gitignored). See `docs/firebase-future.md`.

## Do not

- Add `sequelize.sync({ force: true })` or destructive SQL
- Log or return full plist payloads in production without need
